# The canonical environment file lives in the web app, where Next.js and the
# chain CLI scripts actually read it:
#
#     apps/web/.env.example   → copy to → apps/web/.env
#
#     cd apps/web && cp .env.example .env && pnpm algo:keygen
#
# See docs/ALGORAND.md for the full setup (accounts, faucets, opt-in, settling).
# For the Casper path instead, see docs/TESTNET.md.
#
# Only docker-compose reads anything from this directory, and it has its own
# defaults baked in (Postgres on port 5404); no env needed to run `pnpm db:up`.
